{
  "id": 216277993,
  "iid": 10248,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "MySQL: Support zstd compressed traffic",
  "description": "If `mysql.caps.compress_zsd` is set in the server greeting and in the \"Login Request\" then zstandard is used.\n\nUse `mysql --compression-algorithms=zstd ...` to get a MySQL client session to use zstandard.\n\nNote that we have `mysql.compression.zstd_level` in the \"Login Request\", but this isn't used in `tvb_child_uncompress_zstd()` and that doesn't seem to cause problems for now.\n\nNot sure if the `#ifdef HAVE_ZSTD` is needed as it looks like calling `tvb_uncompress_zstd()` should be ok even without zstd (should return NULL).\n\n[mysql_zstd.pcapng](/uploads/a6ba05bb171a9605f23d49fc877bf172/mysql_zstd.pcapng)",
